<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts" xml:lang="en-US"><voice name="en-us-emma:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully as a neutral English listening examination narrator. Use precise pronunciation and an unhurried but natural pace. After the number, leave a short pause before the next speaker. Do not separate individual words or sound robotic."><p>Number seventeen.</p></mstts:express-as></voice><voice name="en-US-Andrew:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Read this passage slowly, clearly, and carefully for an English listening examination. Use precise pronunciation, an unhurried natural rhythm, and brief natural pauses at sentence boundaries. Keep the tone calm and neutral. Do not separate individual words, sound dramatic, or emphasize information that could reveal the answer."><p>The Riverside Science Center will open its space exhibition this Saturday. The main hall will be available from nine, but the planetarium will remain closed until one because new equipment is being tested. Visitors with morning planetarium tickets may use them for any afternoon show. The cafe and gift shop will operate on their normal schedule.</p></mstts:express-as></voice><voice name="en-us-emma:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully as a neutral English listening examination narrator. Say Question, pause briefly, and then read the final question with precise pronunciation. Do not emphasize any possible answer clue."><p><s>Question.</s><s>What can morning planetarium ticket holders do?</s></p></mstts:express-as></voice></speak>
